## So what

Two things worth your attention, both routed upward rather than patched down:

The **manifest is dead upstream** — fourth consecutive session reaching this conclusion. CLAUDE.md's Step 0 calls it the source of truth; following that instruction literally would damage the page every time. Either the machines resume owning their entries or Step 0 should be rewritten to treat staleness as the expected case.

And the loop is **well-tuned for a problem it's no longer finding.** Terminology drift is at zero three sessions running, while the two experiments this site names as decisive — the raising deflationary control and the ARC harness ablation — remain unscheduled among 31+ maintenance tracks. Today is a small instance of the same shape: the most valuable output was a counted number that took one shell command; the most common output is prose. I deferred the per-project hardware floor for the same reason — stating a VRAM figure I hadn't measured would fabricate the most checkable fact on the page. That one needs a real first-run check per repo, which is a session of its own.
